PROJECT UNDERSTANDING:
We understand that the Cityof Cheyenne is requesting design services for the refined master plan and detailed construction
designofthe overall corridor, to incorporate the location of multiple train cars along the corridor.Through our initial efforts
with the Reed Ave Corridor, we understand the historic locations of the old railway down15th Street and the intent istoplace
the historic train cars as close to this historic alignment as possible.This will require the adjustment of the south curb &
gutter, existing utilities within thestreet, adjusting pedestrian and vehicular streetlight locations and accesses into existing
parking lots and business located throughout the corridor on the south side of1sth Street.Placement of new track sections
will occur only in locations where rail car locations are identified through the master planning process.We will also maintain
the existing driveway locations, pedestrian access points and layout of Gunslinger Park. Our intent is to blend the south
Our scope of workfor this project includes an abbreviated master plan of the overall corridor, from Bent Ave.to the historic
drawing package (60% final construction drawings) with a 95% construction drawing package and final bid documents, to
follow.We also understand the critical timeline that needs to be met to have final drawings and approval.from the City to
meet the City's schedule for delivery of the renovated railcars.
